#: ../../../api/borders.md:1
msgid "Borders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/borders.md:1
msgid "The borders of a range, accessed via `myrange.borders`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/borders.md:3
msgid ""
"Use `set()` to write several attributes in one go or to target a group of "
"sides, and `clear()` to remove borders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.Borders:10
#: xlwings.main.Borders.clear:16 xlwings.main.Borders.set:30
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/borders.md:1
msgid ""
"Returns the native object (`pywin32` or `appscript` obj) of the engine being "
"used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/borders.md:1
msgid "Removes borders. Same as `set(which, line_style=None)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/borders.md:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.Borders.clear:6
msgid ""
"A side name, a list of side names or a group, see :meth:`set() <xlwings.main."
"Borders.set>`. Defaults to ``\"everything\"``, i.e. all eight sides "
"including the diagonals; ``clear(\"all\")`` leaves the diagonals alone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/borders.md:1
msgid ""
"Returns or sets the color of the four edges and the two inside borders, i.e. "
"Excel's \"All Borders\", see {attr}`Border.color <xlwings.main.Border."
"color>`. Reads the common value, or `None` if they differ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/borders.md:0
msgid "Setter type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/borders.md:1
msgid ""
"Fetch the common color of the four edges and the two inside borders on "
"demand, as an RGB tuple."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/borders.md:4
msgid ""
"`None` if they differ. Segments that differ from cell to cell within a side "
"aren't detected on any engine, see {meth}`Border.get_line_style() <xlwings."
"main.Border.get_line_style>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/borders.md:8
msgid "Requires xlwings Lite."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/borders.md:0
msgid "Return type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/borders.md:1
msgid ""
"Fetch the common line style of the four edges and the two inside borders on "
"demand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/borders.md:1
msgid ""
"Fetch the common weight of the four edges and the two inside borders on "
"demand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/borders.md:1
msgid ""
"Returns or sets the line style of the four edges and the two inside borders, "
"i.e. Excel's \"All Borders\", see {attr}`Border.line_style <xlwings.main."
"Border.line_style>`. Reads the common value, or `None` if they differ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/borders.md:1
msgid "Sets one or more attributes on one or more sides in one go."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/borders.md:3
msgid ""
"Only the attributes you pass are written. For each side, they're applied in "
"the order color, weight, line style, so that the line style is what survives "
"when Excel can't represent a combination (for instance, `\"dash_dot_dot\"` "
"with `\"thick\"` reads back as `\"thin\"`). Validation happens before "
"anything is written; if the host rejects a combination, the error propagates "
"and earlier writes stay in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.Borders.set:13
msgid ""
"A side name (``\"edge_top\"``, ...), a list of side names, or one of the "
"groups ``\"outside\"`` (the four edges), ``\"inside\"`` (the two inside "
"borders), ``\"all\"`` (outside + inside, the default) and ``\"everything\"`` "
"(all eight sides, including the diagonals)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.Borders.set:17
msgid ""
"See :attr:`Border.line_style <xlwings.main.Border.line_style>`. ``None`` or "
"``\"none\"`` removes the selected borders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.Borders.set:20
msgid ""
"See :attr:`Border.weight <xlwings.main.Border.weight>`. ``None`` isn't "
"allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.Borders.set:22
msgid ""
"See :attr:`Border.color <xlwings.main.Border.color>`. ``None`` isn't allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/borders.md:1
msgid ""
"Returns or sets the weight of the four edges and the two inside borders, i."
"e. Excel's \"All Borders\", see {attr}`Border.weight <xlwings.main.Border."
"weight>`. Reads the common value, or `None` if they differ."
msgstr ""
